pocket-ui @VERSION@: install on an existing ROCKNIX card (Retroid Pocket Mini V2)
==================================================================================

Also for the Retroid Pocket 5, Retroid Pocket Flip 2 (Snapdragon 865) and the first Retroid Pocket
Mini, as EXPERIMENTAL: they run the same ROCKNIX for SM8250, but pocket-ui has not been tested on
them yet. Most things should work; if something doesn't, Settings -> System -> About -> Report a
problem saves a file you can attach to a report.

pocket-ui is a game launcher with its own libretro frontend. This package puts it on a microSD card
that already runs ROCKNIX, in place of EmulationStation. Your games, saves and ROCKNIX settings stay.
EmulationStation stays installed too: pocket-ui hands over to it if it cannot start, and uninstall.sh
brings it back.

pocket-ui is not made or endorsed by the ROCKNIX team.

New card instead? On a Mini V2 the SD card image (pocket-ui-@VERSION@-rp-mini-v2.img.xz) is the
easier way: it needs no SSH and sets everything up by itself. It is for the Mini V2 only: on the
other devices, install ROCKNIX for your device as ROCKNIX describes, start it once, then use this
package.


No SSH? Use the one file "Install pocket-ui.sh"
-----------------------------------------------

This zip is the way for people who have SSH. Without a terminal, take the single file
"Install pocket-ui.sh" instead (it carries this whole package; it is a separate download next to this zip):

1. Copy "Install pocket-ui.sh" into the folder roms/ports of the card: over ROCKNIX's file sharing
   from your computer, or with the SD card in the computer.
2. In EmulationStation restart the list once (Start -> Game Settings -> Update Gamelists), open
   Ports and start "Install pocket-ui".
3. The screen shows what it checks (nothing is written until every check passed), then the install,
   then the switch. Press Close when it says so; pocket-ui starts. The entry removes itself and
   leaves "Uninstall pocket-ui" in Ports.

If something does not fit (another device, a ROCKNIX older than the tested one, too little space), the screen
says so in a sentence, nothing on the card is changed, and Close takes you back to EmulationStation.
Starting it twice is harmless. It uses the same install.sh as below, unchanged.
Alternative with two files: put this zip next to a copy of the small starter "Install pocket-ui.sh"
(without the package inside) in roms/ports; the starter finds the zip.


You need (the SSH way below)
----------------------------

- A Retroid Pocket Mini V2 (or, experimental, a Retroid Pocket 5, Flip 2 or first Mini) with ROCKNIX
  for SM8250, version @TESTED_ROCKNIX@ or newer, started normally at least once. A newer ROCKNIX is fine when
  pocket-ui's own check passes; an older one is refused ("update ROCKNIX first"), as is another device;
  see "Options" below.
- SSH switched on in ROCKNIX (EmulationStation: Network Settings -> Enable SSH) and a computer on the
  same Wi-Fi. ROCKNIX's login is root, password rocknix unless you changed it.
- About @NEED_MB@ MB free on the card.


Install
-------

1. Copy the zip to the device and unpack it there (replace <device-ip>):

     scp pocket-ui-@VERSION@-rocknix-install.zip root@<device-ip>:/storage/
     ssh root@<device-ip>
     cd /storage && unzip -o pocket-ui-@VERSION@-rocknix-install.zip
     cd pocket-ui-@VERSION@-rocknix-install

2. Check first (changes nothing):

     sh install.sh --check

3. Install:

     sh install.sh

   The checks run again, then the programs go to /storage/pocket-ui and one start entry to
   /storage/.config/system.d/essway.service.d/10-pocket-ui.conf. The interface restarts (a running
   game ends) and pocket-ui opens its first-start setup. Running install.sh again is safe.

After that, every start of the device opens pocket-ui. The package folder and the zip in /storage can
be deleted.


What the checks refuse
----------------------

install.sh changes nothing unless all of these pass:
- the package is complete (files/SHA256SUMS),
- the system is ROCKNIX for SM8250 (aarch64), version @TESTED_ROCKNIX@ or newer,
- the device is a Retroid Pocket Mini V2, or one of the experimental Pocket 5, Flip 2 and first Mini
  (its device tree says so; the experimental ones are noted, not refused),
- ROCKNIX's interface unit (essway) and EmulationStation's start script are there, ROCKNIX's first
  start has run, and there is enough free space on /storage,
- pocket-ui and pocket-core run on this system and print version @VERSION@,
- pocket-ui's own compatibility check of the running system passes (the libraries and their versions
  both programs need, the programs and ROCKNIX scripts they call, the emulator cores).

Options:
  --check                     only the checks
  --no-restart                install, but start pocket-ui only at the next start of the device
  --allow-untested-rocknix    a ROCKNIX older than @TESTED_ROCKNIX@; the compatibility check still has to pass
  --allow-other-device        another SM8250 device pocket-ui doesn't know (untested; the screen layout
                              may not fit)


Uninstall
---------

Without SSH: start "Uninstall pocket-ui" in Ports (the installer leaves it in roms/ports; the file
"Uninstall pocket-ui.sh" is also built next to the installer). With SSH:

  sh /storage/pocket-ui/uninstall.sh

removes the start entry and /storage/pocket-ui, puts back what pocket-ui changed in ROCKNIX's
configuration (its file-sharing settings and Syncthing start entry), and restarts EmulationStation.
pocket-ui's own settings stay in /storage/.config/pocket-ui unless you add --purge. Games and saves
in /storage/roms are never touched. Settings pocket-ui changed in ROCKNIX's system settings (Wi-Fi,
volume, SSH) stay as they are. --keep-programs removes only the start entry.

By hand, the same in one step: delete /storage/.config/system.d/essway.service.d/10-pocket-ui.conf
and restart the device.


Good to know
------------

- Do not install ROCKNIX updates while pocket-ui is on the card unless a pocket-ui release says the
  new version is supported. Run "sh install.sh --check" from a newer pocket-ui package after one.
- Remote access (SSH) stays as ROCKNIX had it. pocket-ui's switch is Settings -> Connections ->
  Remote access.
- The log is /var/log/pocket-ui.log; a copy that survives a restart is in
  /storage/.config/pocket-ui/logs/.


Package contents
----------------

  install.sh, uninstall.sh   the two scripts above (uninstall.sh is also copied to /storage/pocket-ui)
  files/pocket-ui, files/pocket-core   pocket-ui @VERSION@ (aarch64, built from commit @REPO_COMMIT@)
  files/portmaster-setup.sh  PortMaster's first start under pocket-ui
  files/run-pocket-ui.sh     the launcher (restarts after crashes, rolls back, falls back to EmulationStation)
  files/10-pocket-ui.conf    the start entry (a systemd drop-in for ROCKNIX's essway unit)
  files/VERSION, files/SHA256SUMS
  LICENSE, NOTICE.md         pocket-ui's licence and third-party credits
  licences/                  the licence texts that go with the programs: the Rust crates' (THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt,
                             THIRD-PARTY-CRATES.md) and the fonts' (FONTS-OFL.txt); install.sh copies them to
                             /storage/pocket-ui/licences, and Settings -> System -> About names that folder


